README for LuaJIT 2.1
---------------------

## Pandaloop Note
This is a fork of the luajit made by Pandaloop.
This fork is SPECIFICALLY meant for the Pandaloop scenery web framework.
If you want to use this fork in another project be warned that some assumptions the jit compiler
does may be broken and have to be fixed.

The main differences are in syntax.

The only semantic difference is arrays starting at 0.
Because of that some standard functions may be broken but will be fixed ASAP if a problem occurs.

See the [./examples] directory for examples of the new syntax.

This fork is not recommended for use outside of the Pandaloop scenery web framework.
## Continuation of old Readme

LuaJIT is a Just-In-Time (JIT) compiler for the Lua programming language.

Project Homepage: https://luajit.org/

LuaJIT is Copyright (C) 2005-2025 Mike Pall.
LuaJIT is free software, released under the MIT license.
See full Copyright Notice in the COPYRIGHT file or in luajit.h.

Documentation for LuaJIT is available in HTML format.
Please point your favorite browser to:

 doc/luajit.html

